// Model-callable tools for the agent runtime.
//
// A tool is an ordinary function, not a package binding:
//
//     #[agent_tool("Adds two integers")]
//     public async func add(run: Run, args: AddArgs) returns int { ... }
//
// `#[agent_tool("description")]` is the only attribute the language adds. The
// tool name is the function name (project-wide unique), the input schema comes
// from the payload parameter through the JSON derive, and effects and required
// capabilities are read from the IR call graph by `surface --json`. Nothing is
// declared here.
//
// Lowering synthesizes one marshalling wrapper per tool and an idempotent
// registration function per module; the wrapper ABI is frozen in
// `docs/adr/0019-agent-tool-dispatch.md` and the runtime invokes wrappers by
// address through the governed dispatch (`act`, `tool_call`).
//
// There is no tool registry in this package and no native extern declaration:
// the surface is the `#[agent_tool]` attribute plus the compiler's `std.agent`
// declarations.
